---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'About FindATradey | UK Verified Tradesmen Match Service';
const description = 'About FindATradey: a UK trade-finder built around register verification, three-engineers-per-job matching, and a no-spam promise.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="container-prose py-12 prose prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:tracking-tight max-w-none">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-ink-900">About FindATradey</h1>

    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-700">
      FindATradey was built to fix one specific problem: when you search for a tradesman in the UK, you usually get one of two bad outcomes — a national lead-network that sells your number to twenty contractors, or a thin directory listing tradesmen who haven't updated their profile since 2014.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Our promise</h2>

    <ul class="mt-3 text-ink-700">
      <li>You get <strong>three named engineers</strong>, not twenty</li>
      <li>Every engineer is <strong>verified weekly</strong> against the relevant UK register (Gas Safe, NICEIC, NAPIT, ELECSA, OFTEC, MCS)</li>
      <li>Your phone number is <strong>shared with one engineer</strong> — the one who claims your job — not all three</li>
      <li>Once your job is done, <strong>we don't ring you again</strong></li>
      <li>The service is <strong>free</strong> for homeowners. Engineers pay only when they win the job.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">What we do</h2>

    <p class="text-ink-700">
      For each UK postcode district we cover, we maintain a verified roster of trade engineers across the categories we publish (plumber, electrician, heating engineer). When you submit your job, we ring the closest, fastest-responding and best-reviewed engineers in our roster, brief them on your job, and only release your contact details to the engineer who confirms they can take it. Lead refunds are automatic if the engineer can't deliver.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">What we don't do</h2>

    <p class="text-ink-700">
      We don't sell your details to lead-network aggregators. We don't run referral kickbacks with insurers. We don't make money from your data. The only way we earn is the engineer paying us a fixed fee on a converted job.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">How we make sure tradesmen show up</h2>

    <p class="text-ink-700">
      Engineers who don't reply to us within an hour drop out of our roster. Engineers who quote and don't deliver get one warning, then are removed. Engineers who get poor reviews from the homeowners we sent them to get removed. The roster gets stronger over time because the bad actors don't survive in it.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-8 text-ink-700">
      <a href="/how-we-vet-tradesmen/" class="text-brand-700">Read more about how we vet tradesmen →</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
